  "title": "TWAMP: Fix sender timestamp format (Z-bit, RFC 8186)",
  "description": "The Z-bit being 1 indicates truncated PTP time format according to\nRFC 8186. Zero (as it must be prior to that) indicates NTP time format.\nThe handling was reversed for one of the three cases.",
