      "title": "TWAMP: Fix sender timestamp format (Z-bit, RFC 8186)",
      "message": "TWAMP: Fix sender timestamp format (Z-bit, RFC 8186)\n\nThe Z-bit being 1 indicates truncated PTP time format according to\nRFC 8186. Zero (as it must be prior to that) indicates NTP time format.\nThe handling was reversed for one of the three cases.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-10-03T21:15:14.000-04:00",
